    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0705" n="629" xml:id="pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/110</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Silliman </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-24T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 24, 1915, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 22, 6 p.m., relative bank situation. Parker being instructed to
                    repeat to you lengthy telegram on this matter. Immediately upon its receipt lay
                    matter before Carranza and urgently request, in view of the serious consequences
                    that may result from the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government’s
                    attitude in this matter, that the banks be given sufficient time to meet the
                    requirements of the order.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
